name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q2_2026'

question 'On a restaurant ordering page, clicking "Place Order" makes a confirmation message appear without reloading the page. Which sequence describes what happened inside the app?'

wrong 'JavaScript loaded the entire page from the server, then showed the confirmation.'
wrong 'The confirmation was always on the page — clicking just scrolled to it.'
right 'The event listener detected the click, the event handler ran, and JavaScript updated the DOM to display the confirmation.'
wrong 'The server pushed the confirmation message to the page before the user clicked.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

